Monitor HPE Networking (Aruba) Instant On switches and access points
from the OPNsense web interface.

The plugin reads, and never changes:

* Instant On 1930/1960 switches in local management mode: ports, link
  speed, throughput, errors, PoE per port and budget, VLANs, LLDP
  neighbours, MAC address table, temperature, fans, power supply and
  the switch log.
* Instant On access points through their local diagnostic page:
  model, firmware, swarm coordinator, cloud and time-sync status and
  the reason of the last restart.
* Optionally the Instant On cloud portal: SSIDs, signal and band of
  wireless clients, radios and alerts.

Clients are correlated with the firewall ARP table, DHCP leases and
static mappings. Health checks point out problems such as a wrong
switch clock, failing time sync, unstable ports, crashed access points
or PoE faults, and changes are recorded as events and sent to syslog.

